Logic:

if ctx.mode in ("paper", "live"): call fetch_orderbook_snapshot(symbol). If it succeeds, compute real imbalance via compute_imbalance, tag dataQuality: "real_orderbook". If the fetch fails (network error, rate limit, symbol not found), fall back to the proxy path below rather than raising or returning garbage — a transient Binance API hiccup during a live tick must never crash the bot's execution loop, matching the same resilience principle already established for fetch_latest_candle's error handling in binance_ingest.py.
else (historical/walk-forward/monte-carlo, or paper/live fetch failure): compute the OHLCV-derived proxy from ctx.candle (open/high/low/close/volume), tag dataQuality: "proxy_from_ohlcv".
Never let this node's output be silently indistinguishable between the two paths — dataQuality must always be present and correct.
